            {
              "id": "2a18fc1b-6c79-34c7-9aff-566882e7aa48",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the code is flagged as an undefined behavior risk due to the absence of explicit checks for null pointers on either the source or destination buffers. The analysis indicates that the destination buffer may be null at the point of the call, which could lead to a crash or other unpredictable behavior if the function is invoked with a null destination. The source buffer is guarded and cannot be null, but the lack of a guard for the destination is a significant risk. The function call does not use a count value derived from the destination's capacity, and there is no explicit null-terminator assignment after the copy, which further increases the risk. The probability of this being a false positive is very low due to these factors.\n\n## In Context Remediation 1\nBefore calling the copy operation, ensure that the destination buffer is not null. This can be done by adding an explicit check for the destination pointer. If the destination is null, handle the error appropriately (e.g., return an error code or log the issue).\n\n```c\nif (next != NULL && next->str != NULL) {\n    strncpy(next->str, str, FLIGHT_RECORDER_ENTRY_STRLEN);\n    next->str[FLIGHT_RECORDER_ENTRY_STRLEN - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n} else {\n    // Handle error: destination buffer is null\n}\n```\n\n\n## In Context Remediation 2\nIf the structure containing the destination buffer is dynamically allocated, ensure that allocation is successful before using the buffer. For example:\n\n```c\nnext = malloc(sizeof(*next));\nif (next == NULL || next->str == NULL) {\n    // Handle allocation failure\n} else {\n    strncpy(next->str, str, FLIGHT_RECORDER_ENTRY_STRLEN);\n    next->str[FLIGHT_RECORDER_ENTRY_STRLEN - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n}\n```\n\n\n## In Context Remediation 3\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS111237"
                ]
              }
