            {
              "id": "fe7c5895-2c12-3023-ab1f-fc5967bddb57",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis detected a possible undefined behavior risk due to overlapping memory regions in a memory copy operation. The destination and source memory areas may overlap, as indicated by the dataflow analysis, which can lead to unpredictable results when using memcpy. Additionally, the source pointer may be null, which could cause a crash. There are no explicit checks or guards in the code to prevent these issues, and the function verdict confirms this as a genuine issue. The risk is further increased because the destination and source are not clearly separated, and the size of the copy is not derived from the destination's capacity.\n\n## In Context Remediation 1\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory regions that may overlap, add a runtime check to ensure the source and destination do not overlap before calling memcpy. If overlap is possible, use memmove instead, which is safe for overlapping regions.\n\n```c\nif (((char*)va_start + bytes_after_wrap <= (char*)&tmp_pkt[bytes_before_wrap]) ||\n    ((char*)&tmp_pkt[bytes_before_wrap] + bytes_after_wrap <= (char*)va_start)) {\n    // No overlap, safe to use memcpy\n    memcpy((void*)&tmp_pkt[bytes_before_wrap], (void*)va_start, bytes_after_wrap);\n} else {\n    // Overlap detected, use memmove\n    memmove((void*)&tmp_pkt[bytes_before_wrap], (void*)va_start, bytes_after_wrap);\n}\n```\n\n\n## In Context Remediation 2\nAlternatively, replace memcpy with memmove directly if you cannot guarantee that the source and destination do not overlap. memmove is designed to handle overlapping memory regions safely.\n\n```c\nmemmove((void*)&tmp_pkt[bytes_before_wrap], (void*)va_start, bytes_after_wrap);\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n\n___\n"
              },
